{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OBSERVATION\nAlready had RCA; I verified the specimen. infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh classifies mergedness solely with git merge-base --is-ancestor rev main_sha. Locally, origin/main=53d18aad..., specimen tip 9c3c5ba2ea21 exists but git merge-base --is-ancestor 9c3c5ba2ea21 origin/main returns rc=1. The same tip's Change-Id Ic469bc5d6262e0be2680f0e0da17fbe3026241 is present on origin/main as 2e131f2071a0 with the same subject/body. Thus the script would label the branch ABANDONED? although the change landed under a different SHA.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nThe mechanism is SHA-ancestry identity in infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh, not content/change identity. Gerrit's Rebase-If-Necessary submit can rewrite the submitted commit SHA, so the pre-submit branch tip is not an ancestor of main even when the branch's work is integrated. Branches that merged without SHA rewrite are classified correctly; rebased-on-submit branches are false negatives.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nThe bounded experiment used local git object/history queries only: ancestor_rc=1, both commits present, same Change-Id found in main under 2e131f2071a0. Evidence that would disprove the RCA would be the tip being an ancestor, or no equivalent Change-Id/content in main; neither held. The prior ticket comment also identified a working in-repo comparison: rebar-worktree-gc.sh already uses a two-tier ancestry then byte-identity predicate.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nDesign-free adoption candidate: keep is-ancestor as MERGED-BACK fast path, then fall back to the GC's touched-file byte-identity/content-equivalence check and report MERGED-REBASED separately from NOT-IN-MAIN. Also document that deletion is age/owner driven or gate deletion on state."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788737915684450001,"uuid":"f6b26678-c978-48f5-b71f-78bf14c0dff7"}